## Summary

`scene.open('model.obj')` returns a scene with an empty mesh (named `STL_Node`) for a valid OBJ file whose first line is a comment or an `o` line. The format detection in `Scene.openFromBuffer` recognises OBJ only when the first 100 characters contain `mtllib` or `usemtl`, or begin with `v` followed by a number; every other text file falls through to the STL importer, which finds no facets and raises no error.

## Environment

- Revision `66cb26df3b031f0bf6976d4e88dc89721983afa4` (default branch `master`)
- Node.js v22.23.3 and npm 10.9.9 (Docker image `node:22-slim`, Linux); the same results on Windows with Node.js v22.11.0
- `npm install` and `npm run build` complete without errors; verified on 2026-10-16

## Steps to reproduce

```sh
npm install
npm run build
node repro.js   # repro.js holds the script below, saved in the repository root
```

```js
const fs = require('fs');
const { Scene } = require('./dist/aspose/threed');
const { Mesh } = require('./dist/aspose/threed/entities');
const { Vector4 } = require('./dist/aspose/threed/utilities');

function triangle() {
  const mesh = new Mesh('tri');
  mesh.controlPoints = [new Vector4(10, 20, 30, 1), new Vector4(11, 20, 30, 1), new Vector4(10, 21, 30, 1)];
  mesh.createPolygon(0, 1, 2);
  return mesh;
}

fs.writeFileSync('model.obj', '# exported by a tool\no Tri\nv 0 0 0\nv 1 0 0\nv 0 1 0\nf 1 2 3\n');

const scene = new Scene();
scene.open('model.obj');
const node = scene.rootNode.childNodes[0];
console.log(node.name, 'control points:', node.entity.controlPoints.length, 'polygons:', node.entity.polygonCount);
```

## Expected

The scene holds a mesh with 3 control points and 1 polygon, as it does when the same file starts with `v 0 0 0` or `mtllib x.mtl`.

## Actual result

```
STL_Node control points: 0 polygons: 0
```
No exception is thrown.

## Where in the repository

- `src/aspose/threed/Scene.ts:161`: only the first 100 characters are examined
- `src/aspose/threed/Scene.ts:172`: `content.includes('mtllib') || content.includes('usemtl') || content.match(/^v\s+-?\d/)` is the whole OBJ test
- `src/aspose/threed/Scene.ts:216-221`: the fallback is `StlImporter`

